From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tvrtko Ursulin <tvrtko.ursulin@igalia.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 09:43:24 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 050/117] drm/sched: Do not overaccount job runtime
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Currently the starting timestamp of the next job on the timeline is
adjusted to the end of a preceding job. This works if the next job has
been submitted while the preceding job was still executing, but not if it
was submitted in the window between it finishing and free job work running
the timestamp adjustment.

This can happen because the run job and free job work items share the same
ordered workqueue and run job can easily submit the next job before the
free job gets a chance to run. This over accounting window is present
especially with single credit schedulers, but not limited too.

Fix it by only adjusting the starting timestamp if it is not already after
the finish time of the preceding job.

While at it move the logic to a helper to keep indendation at bay.

Signed-off-by: Tvrtko Ursulin <tvrtko.ursulin@igalia.com>
Fixes: 1774baa64f93 ("drm/scheduler: Change scheduled fence track v2")
Cc: Christian König <christian.koenig@amd.com>
Cc: Danilo Krummrich <dakr@kernel.org>
Cc: Matthew Brost <matthew.brost@intel.com>
Cc: Philipp Stanner <phasta@kernel.org>
Acked-by: Philipp Stanner <phasta@kernel.org>

[mzak: picked for q91o (21 Nov gains plan) from patchwork series 1213682; mark C; ported onto the dma-fence timestamp ordering series (pw 1216171): comparison done under the scheduled fence lock in drm_sched_overwrite_scheduled_timestamp()]

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: mzak <mzak.amin@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/scheduler/sched_main.c | 17 ++++++++++++++---
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/scheduler/sched_main.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/scheduler/sched_main.c
index 7f2a534d08513..68ed8af9efe51 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/scheduler/sched_main.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/scheduler/sched_main.c
@@ -903,16 +903,27 @@ drm_sched_select_entity(struct drm_gpu_scheduler *sched)
  * drm_sched_overwrite_scheduled_timestamp - make timestamp more accurate
  *
  * Overwrites the timestamp of the provided scheduled fence with the one from
- * the finished fence, if the scheduled fence is already signaled. Does nothing
- * otherwise.
+ * the finished fence, if the scheduled fence is already signaled and the
+ * finished timestamp is the later one. Does nothing otherwise.
  */
 static void
 drm_sched_overwrite_scheduled_timestamp(struct dma_fence *finished,
 					struct dma_fence *scheduled)
 {
 	ktime_t timestamp = dma_fence_timestamp(finished);
+	unsigned long flags;
 
-	dma_fence_overwrite_timestamp(scheduled, timestamp);
+	/*
+	 * If the next job has been submitted while the previous one was still
+	 * running adjust its starting timestamp to avoid accounting overlap.
+	 * Never move it back: a job submitted after the previous one finished
+	 * keeps its own start.
+	 */
+	dma_fence_lock_irqsave(scheduled, flags);
+	if (dma_fence_test_signaled_flag(scheduled) &&
+	    ktime_after(timestamp, scheduled->timestamp))
+		scheduled->timestamp = timestamp;
+	dma_fence_unlock_irqrestore(scheduled, flags);
 }
 
